{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"captious-beefwitted-pterosaurs","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nMove the production bridge wrapper logic into one runner-neutral Python entrypoint and keep provider\nworkflows thin. This is an additive migration: checked-out workflows and environments that still\ninvoke `rebar reconcile --mode ...` remain supported with their existing defaults, messages,\nmutation boundaries, and legacy 3/4/75 results.\n\nThe runner accepts the existing `MODE` vocabulary at this compatibility boundary. It preserves\nthese routes exactly:\n\n- `reconcile-check` invokes legacy `rebar reconcile --mode reconcile-check`.\n- `dry-run` invokes canonical `rebar bridge preview`.\n- `bootstrap-strict` invokes canonical `rebar bridge sync --max-changes 10`.\n- `bootstrap-throttle` invokes canonical `rebar bridge sync --max-changes 100`.\n- `live` invokes uncapped canonical `rebar bridge sync`.\n\nThe runner owns the required environment-name set, the 3600-second timeout, and the canonical\n0/1/2 provider result. It derives allowed results from\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py::_Disposition`. It translates legacy benign\n3/4/75 only at this wrapper boundary. Direct legacy callers continue to observe those values.\n\nAfter a successful non-paused pass, delivery uses this complete command contract:\n\n```text\nREBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always python -m rebar._store.push commit-and-push \\\n  --tracker .tickets-tracker \\\n  --message \"chore: sync events from rebar reconciler [run <BRIDGE_RUN_ID>]\" \\\n  --strict \\\n  --author-name \"$BRIDGE_BOT_NAME\" \\\n  --author-email \"$BRIDGE_BOT_EMAIL\"\n```\n\n`<BRIDGE_RUN_ID>` is the validated provider-supplied `BRIDGE_RUN_ID`. A missing required identity or\nrun id is invalid invocation and exits 2 before reconciliation. Delivery failure exits 1 and keeps\nthe subprocess diagnostic. A valid exact `BRIDGE_PAUSED: <json>` marker exits 0 without delivery.\n\nThe GitHub Actions, Jenkins, and GitLab configs retain only provider-native checkout/bootstrap,\ncredential and signing-key materialization, masking, artifacts/notifications, scheduling, timeout,\nand canonical result mapping. GitHub Actions retains its existing 20-minute schedule and opt-in\n`RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS` re-dispatch. Jenkins and GitLab use native schedulers.\n\nGitLab portability is a required contract artifact. Vendor GitLab's Draft-07 CI schema from\n`gitlab-org/gitlab/app/assets/javascripts/editor/schema/ci.json` at immutable commit\n`776c20ad5675eecea0c2010433a94d98d745e921`. Before committing it, retrieve the immutable raw URL,\nrecompute SHA-256, confirm the document dialect, and record URL, revision, retrieval date, dialect,\nand checksum in adjacent provenance. Offline tests validate `.gitlab-ci.yml` against that vendored\nschema.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Inventory the production workflow and every parser/lint/policy test that consumes it.\n2. Add RED-first happy, edge, and end-to-end tests for the real runner and provider wrappers.\n3. Physically hold out edge and end-to-end tests from the implementation worker.\n4. Implement `scripts/run_reconcile_bridge.py` and thin provider wrappers.\n5. Pin `shellcheck-py==0.11.0.1`; validate extracted wrapper shell bodies without skips.\n6. Retarget existing workflow tests without discarding legacy-continuity assertions.\n7. Update user and release documentation with noun-based primary usage plus retained legacy usage.\n8. Run focused tests, schema validation, lint, typecheck, module-size, and full project gates.\n\nNo contention harness is required: the runner invokes existing locked store/reconciler seams and\nadds no retry, cache, snapshot, or composed check-then-act store mutation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `scripts/run_reconcile_bridge.py` is the sole runner-neutral bridge wrapper.\n- [ ] The runner accepts all five existing `MODE` values.\n- [ ] Each existing `MODE` value maps to the specified legacy or canonical route.\n- [ ] Direct legacy reconcile callers retain their published 3/4/75 results.\n- [ ] The runner translates benign 3/4/75 results to provider result 0.\n- [ ] The runner preserves operational result 1.\n- [ ] The runner preserves invalid-invocation result 2.\n- [ ] A valid exact `BRIDGE_PAUSED` marker exits 0.\n- [ ] A paused pass skips ticket-store delivery.\n- [ ] Every successful non-paused pass invokes the complete strict delivery command.\n- [ ] `BRIDGE_RUN_ID` appears in the required delivery commit message.\n- [ ] Bridge bot name and email are passed to strict delivery.\n- [ ] Strict-delivery failure exits 1 with its diagnostic preserved.\n- [ ] A true shallow repository exits 2 before reconciliation.\n- [ ] Shallow rejection prints the specified compatibility diagnostic.\n- [ ] The GitHub Actions wrapper invokes the shared runner.\n- [ ] The GitHub Actions 20-minute schedule remains unchanged.\n- [ ] The opt-in `RECONCILE_CONTINUOUS` re-dispatch remains supported.\n- [ ] The Jenkins wrapper invokes the shared runner.\n- [ ] The GitLab wrapper invokes the shared runner.\n- [ ] Provider wrappers are contract-checked against runner-owned secrets and timeout constants.\n- [ ] Provider result mappings are checked against `_Disposition` through the runner constants.\n- [ ] The vendored GitLab schema has verified immutable provenance and checksum metadata.\n- [ ] `.gitlab-ci.yml` validates offline against the vendored Draft-07 schema.\n- [ ] Pinned ShellCheck 0.11.0 lints extracted shell bodies from all three provider configs.\n- [ ] Missing or mismatched ShellCheck fails setup instead of skipping validation.\n- [ ] A five-environment matrix proves identical runner output, result, and ref effects.\n- [ ] The five-environment matrix runs with vendor variables scrubbed and `gh` absent.\n- [ ] Existing workflow parsing, lint, partial-clone, identity, and main-push policy tests pass.\n- [ ] Documentation presents noun-based bridge commands as primary.\n- [ ] Documentation identifies legacy reconcile commands as supported compatibility entrypoints.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `scripts/run_reconcile_bridge.py`\n- `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`\n- `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`\n- `Jenkinsfile`\n- `.gitlab-ci.yml`\n- `.github/schemas/gitlab-ci.schema.json`\n- `.github/schemas/gitlab-ci.schema.provenance.json`\n- `pyproject.toml`\n- `uv.lock`\n- `tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py`\n- `tests/scripts/test_reconcile_bridge_push_retry.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_merge_driver.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py`\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_primary_workflow_heldout.py`\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_actionlint_scope.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_partial_clone_workflows.py`\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_run_pass_lock_lost_exit.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_workflow_names.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_check_dco_identity.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py`\n- focused new runner/provider contract tests\n- `docs/user-guide.md`","id":"8b08-e4d7-8dca-4aa6","parent_id":"2db2-3f5e-cf3a-464c","priority":1,"tags":["bridge","portability","ci"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Extract a runner-neutral bridge entrypoint and thin CI wrappers"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786404919211116001,"uuid":"9a7d7d9b-393b-4b09-9391-55bef0edd791"}